1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,788
Every trader has their own way of reading a chart.

2
00:00:02,808 --> 00:00:05,804
Angstrom Lattice lets you write yours down once,

3
00:00:05,854 --> 00:00:08,351
and have it checked on every asset you follow.

4
00:00:08,788 --> 00:00:12,373
It starts with signals: the indicators behind the dashboard,

5
00:00:12,393 --> 00:00:14,596
such as moving averages, RSI, volume,

6
00:00:14,616 --> 00:00:17,920
and market structure. Each one measures one thing.

7
00:00:18,357 --> 00:00:20,987
Signal Groups combine signals into one reading,

8
00:00:21,007 --> 00:00:24,182
a score from minus one hundred to plus one hundred,

9
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:26,403
with labels you choose, such as Bullish.

10
00:00:26,423 --> 00:00:28,648
The dashboard's already configured Trend,

11
00:00:28,668 --> 00:00:31,487
Stretch and Flow are Signal Groups like these.

12
00:00:31,926 --> 00:00:34,658
Signal Sets turn readings into a decision:

13
00:00:34,708 --> 00:00:36,501
Yes, No, or Unknown,

14
00:00:36,551 --> 00:00:40,563
with the line that decided it. For example: the trend is bullish,

15
00:00:40,613 --> 00:00:44,327
and Stochastic is at most thirty, a pullback in an uptrend.

16
00:00:44,778 --> 00:00:47,553
Prism Scan runs a Set across your watchlist,

17
00:00:47,603 --> 00:00:48,649
now,

18
00:00:48,699 --> 00:00:50,386
at a past moment,

19
00:00:50,436 --> 00:00:52,037
or on a schedule.

20
00:00:52,477 --> 00:00:55,209
And when an asset turns Yes, you hear about it,

21
00:00:55,259 --> 00:00:57,671
instantly or in your daily summary.

22
00:00:58,135 --> 00:01:02,702
Strategies come next: entries, exits, and risk, built on the same Sets.

23
00:01:03,149 --> 00:01:06,222
Why it helps: your rules stay the same every time,

24
00:01:06,272 --> 00:01:08,514
every answer shows its reasons,

25
00:01:08,564 --> 00:01:11,978
and missing data is reported as Unknown, never guessed.

26
00:01:12,688 --> 00:01:15,484
Everything here describes the market as it is.

27
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:18,074
It is not a forecast, and not advice.
